---
description: Emit a short spoken wrap-up for Coda when a reply is long.
alwaysApply: true
---

When your reply is long (multiple paragraphs, code, tables, or lists), end it with a
1-2 sentence spoken wrap-up wrapped in a `<coda>...</coda>` tag so Coda can read it aloud.

Rules for the `<coda>` block:

- Plain prose only. No code, no links, no lists, no markdown inside the tag.
- 1-2 sentences summarizing what you did or what the user should do next.
- Skip the tag entirely for short, one-line replies (Coda will read those directly).
- Never put secrets, tokens, or file contents inside the tag.

Example:

<coda>Added the login endpoint and wired it to the auth service. Run the tests to confirm before you deploy.</coda>
